# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the endpoint.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so your real URL never ends up in the repository.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser — and anything
# it does expose is public, so never put a secret or an API key here.

# Where RSVPs go. Leave it blank or delete the line and the invitation falls
# back to localStorage, which is what you want while designing.
#
# The endpoint answers two calls:
#   GET  -> [{ id, name, phone, attendance, guests, message, at }, ...]
#   POST -> one entry in that shape, as a JSON body
#
# `attendance` is "hadir" or "tidak-hadir"; `guests` is 0 for "tidak-hadir".
#
# For Google Apps Script this is the /exec URL of the deployed web app.
# See "RSVP and the guestbook" in README.md for the script and the deploy steps.
VITE_RSVP_ENDPOINT=

# Restart `npm run dev` after changing anything in here — Vite reads env files
# at startup, so an edit will not hot-reload.
